  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Creating a pathway to resilience: paving the way for sustainable reintegration of displaced populations in the Syrian Arab RepublicCreating a pathway to resilience: paving the way for sustainable reintegration of displaced populations in the Syrian Arab Republic</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In response to the shifting context in Syria following the fall of the previous regime in December 2024, IOM is implementing a comprehensive initiative to support evidence-based planning and programming for sustainable returns and reintegration of displaced Syrians. The project addresses critical data gaps and operational challenges by establishing an integrated Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) system in Syria and providing complementary assistance, and conducting a longitudinal return intention survey among Syrians residing in Sweden.</narrative>
  </description>
